      "summary": "The identity and alert configuration includes scoped grants and owner routing checks. The review path still emits an investigation completion event with placeholder model, tool, and citation data, so it does not meet M-08's real-trace requirement.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Auth/CaseEndpoints.cs",
          "line": 69,
          "message": "The review endpoint emits a placeholder investigation trace instead of correlating data from a real investigation.",
          "confidence": 0.93,
          "category": "logic-error",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "After a review is recorded, RecordReview builds an investigation.completed trace using the case revision, the literal model value \"not-invoked\", and empty tool and citation lists.",
            "failureScenario": "When a human review is recorded without a model investigation, telemetry reports an investigation as completed but contains no actual model, tools, or citations. The emitted trace therefore does not correlate the real investigation data required by M-08."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "agentId": "test-reviewer-codex",
      "reviewType": "testing",
      "harness": "codex",
      "harnessVersion": "0.162.0",
      "model": "gpt-6-luna",
      "approved": false,
      "findings": {
        "critical": 0,
        "major": 2,
        "minor": 0,
        "suggestion": 0
      },
      "summary": "The Terraform tests cover several identity and alert behaviors, but the reader-access test does not detect widened or misbound access. The app-path trace test also passes without verifying that its correlation fields come from a real investigation.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "infra/terraform/tests/identity-telemetry.tftest.hcl",
          "line": 305,
          "message": "M-07's reader test does not catch a widened scope or a grant to the wrong group.",
          "confidence": 0.92,
          "category": "testing",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The M-07 reader test checks the Log Analytics Reader role and Group principal type, but does not assert the assignment scope or that its principal_id matches telemetry_reader_group_id.",
            "failureScenario": "If the reader assignment is widened to the resource group or attached to a different group, the test still passes, even though access to telemetry is no longer restricted to the configured reader group."
          }
        },
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api.Tests/TelemetryPrivacyTests.cs",
          "line": 322,
          "message": "M-08's app-path test accepts a placeholder review trace as a real investigation trace.",
          "confidence": 0.91,
          "category": "testing",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The app-path test calls the review endpoint, while RecordReview constructs a trace with model `not-invoked` and empty tools and citation lists. The test checks that the model is nonempty and that tools and citations keys exist, not that they reflect an investigation that ran.",
            "failureScenario": "If the application continues emitting this placeholder trace with no model invocation, tools, or citations, the test passes. M-08 requires a real investigation trace correlated with those fields."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
